			],
			"Message": "docs(Echo): Add field labels, Returns/Errors doc sections across Queue, Scheduler, Task modules\n\nContinue the Rustdoc standards pass from commit 9276508 with two remaining patterns:\n\n- **Field labels** — Prefix all struct fields and enum variants with a bold label (e.g., `High — ...`, `Injector — ...`, `Identifier — ...`, `Operation — ...`) following the `Label — Description` convention, applied across `Priority` (Task), `Priority` (Queue), `Share`, `Context`, `Concurrency`, and `Task`\n- **Doc sections** — Add `## Parameters` on `StealingQueue::Submit()`, `## Returns` on `SchedulerBuilder` builder methods (`Create`, `WithWorkerCount`, `WithQueue`) and `Worker::Create`, and `## Errors` on `Scheduler::Stop()` documenting its non-propagating error log behaviour\n- **Expanded docs** — Extend `Worker::Run` doc to explain the loop exit condition (shutdown via `Scheduler::Stop` or drop)\n- **Tighter module blurb** — Rewrite `Queue/mod.rs` from expository to declarative voice\n\nNo functional changes — documentation only.",
