			"Message": "docs(Echo): Add Key Dependencies, Security, and Compatibility sections to README\n\nExpand the README with three new reference sections that document Echo's crate-level dependencies, security architecture (Safe Rust, structured shutdown, bounded concurrency, decoupled design), and compatibility targets (Mountain, Common, any Tokio-based runtime).\n\nMinor refinements: normalize the System Architecture heading with em-quad spacing, change the Connection Paths table header from \"Mechanism\" to \"Protocol\" for accuracy, bold the API Reference link, and reflow the Funding paragraph for consistent line width.\n\nThese are documentation-only changes with no functional impact on the library.",
